message: "If you use BioEng-TermBench, please cite it as below."
title: "BioEng-TermBench: physics-aware graders for AI agents on biomedical engineering tasks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mbote
    given-names: Samuel Ngigi
    email: mbotesamuel9@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2319-8873"
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23308638
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mbote-droid/bioeng-termbench"
abstract: >-
  Five terminal tasks from biomedical engineering (ECG signal processing,
  pharmacokinetic fitting and dosing, closed-loop insulin delivery, thermal
  ablation planning, debugging a pharmacokinetics package) in the Harbor
  format, with graders that check engineering correctness: units,
  conservation, order of accuracy, safety at the true parameters and
  robustness under uncertainty. The graders are validated with independent
  reference solutions, realistic wrong solutions, grader mutation testing and
  a red team against the grading sandbox.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - benchmark
  - reward hacking
  - grader validation
  - biomedical engineering
  - pharmacokinetics
  - closed-loop control
  - bioheat transfer
  - scientific computing
  - GPU
